WEBVTT

00:48.600 --> 00:50.540
Yes!

00:59.100 --> 01:02.610
After becoming champion and
defending my title a few times,

01:03.180 --> 01:06.010
I think I'm beginning to understand
what it means to be strong...

01:06.010 --> 01:06.930
Dad.

01:09.890 --> 01:11.670
Dad!

01:14.740 --> 01:16.370
Hiroko, Ippo!

02:37.050 --> 02:42.010
The Strongest Challenger

02:40.730 --> 02:42.010
Well, I'm off.

02:42.010 --> 02:44.780
Have a good day. Be careful!

02:44.780 --> 02:45.500
Sure thing!

02:46.220 --> 02:47.390
Hey, Ippo!

02:47.960 --> 02:49.600
Wait, Dad!

02:51.180 --> 02:53.230
Here, you forgot this!

02:53.230 --> 02:54.980
Oh, thank you!

02:56.940 --> 02:59.610
Just wait, I'll bring back a huge haul!

02:59.610 --> 03:02.630
Dad, when you get back, I'll help you!

03:02.630 --> 03:04.310
You will, huh?

03:04.310 --> 03:05.540
It's a promise, then!

03:05.540 --> 03:07.250
Yup, promise!

03:13.430 --> 03:15.290
When's Dad coming home?

03:16.420 --> 03:19.370
Hmm, maybe a week or so?

03:19.370 --> 03:22.180
Be a good boy and he'll
be home in no time!

03:28.860 --> 03:31.020
Sakuma, where are you?!

03:32.060 --> 03:34.520
Makunouchi, get on the raft!

03:34.520 --> 03:36.000
Hurry!

03:36.000 --> 03:39.320
You idiots! Sakuma's still on the boat!

03:40.420 --> 03:42.840
Sakuma, where are you?!

03:43.260 --> 03:44.730
Answer me!

03:45.660 --> 03:46.710
Sakuma!

03:49.470 --> 03:50.570
Makunouchi...

03:50.570 --> 03:51.590
You okay?

03:51.590 --> 03:53.970
Forget about me, it's too late!

03:53.970 --> 03:54.930
Don't say that!

03:54.930 --> 03:57.840
My leg's trapped! I'm done for!

03:59.260 --> 04:00.770
Don't you quit on me.

04:05.450 --> 04:07.470
Forget it, Makunouchi.

04:07.470 --> 04:09.350
Save yourself!

04:14.780 --> 04:18.480
Don't give up! We're all
going home together!

04:19.810 --> 04:21.200
Get him!

04:22.380 --> 04:24.050
Hurry up! Get on the raft!

04:24.050 --> 04:24.860
Move!

04:26.540 --> 04:29.080
Makunouchi!

04:31.680 --> 04:34.040
I will make it home!

04:34.040 --> 04:36.090
Hiroko, Ippo...

04:37.210 --> 04:40.710
Ippo!

04:53.320 --> 04:54.640
He was the best.

04:55.030 --> 04:58.140
Makunouchi was the pride of all fishermen.

04:58.610 --> 05:00.540
Thank you.

05:00.540 --> 05:03.610
Kazuo-san would consider that
the greatest of compliments.

05:03.610 --> 05:05.960
I'm the one who should be thanking him!

05:18.230 --> 05:20.050
Why, if it isn't Ippo!

05:20.050 --> 05:21.210
Mister Sakuma!

05:22.270 --> 05:26.290
Can you show me how to do something?

05:26.290 --> 05:28.860
I sure can.
What do you wanna know?

05:28.860 --> 05:31.220
Teach me how to tie a clove hitch!

05:31.220 --> 05:32.940
A clove hitch?

05:32.940 --> 05:34.600
You gonna moor a ship to the dock?

05:35.060 --> 05:38.230
I wanna learn how to do it
before my dad gets back.

05:38.230 --> 05:40.110
I promised to help him
when he comes home!

05:40.650 --> 05:43.480
When he gets back... you...

05:43.860 --> 05:45.490
Show me!

05:47.030 --> 05:51.100
F-Forget that! How about
an amusement park?

05:51.100 --> 05:53.050
I'll take you anywhere you want to go.

05:53.050 --> 05:54.920
Let's go somewhere fun!

05:54.920 --> 05:57.370
Thank you, but I promised him.

05:57.370 --> 05:59.130
Listen, Ippo...

05:59.680 --> 06:02.770
I know you're young, so maybe
you don't understand,

06:02.770 --> 06:05.510
but your father...

06:06.000 --> 06:09.010
He said he'd come home.

06:10.240 --> 06:12.560
Dad keeps his promises.

06:13.050 --> 06:15.560
He's out there doing the
best he can on his own,

06:15.560 --> 06:17.020
but he'll come back!

06:18.390 --> 06:22.770
A-Anyway, you don't want
to worry your mother!

06:22.770 --> 06:24.410
Let's get you home!

06:24.410 --> 06:25.900
No!

06:26.410 --> 06:30.080
Dad's coming back.
I have to wait for him!

06:38.710 --> 06:39.830
Ippo.

06:40.760 --> 06:42.210
I'm gonna wait a little longer.

06:45.630 --> 06:46.710
Let's go home.

06:49.340 --> 06:51.220
Mom, look!

06:51.660 --> 06:54.220
I learned to tie a bowline knot!

06:54.220 --> 06:54.800
Dad will—

06:54.800 --> 06:56.850
Just come home now, Ippo!

06:59.350 --> 07:03.860
There's no point in waiting
anymore! Your father's not...

07:08.210 --> 07:10.370
Dad keeps his promises.

07:12.110 --> 07:13.820
I know he'll come back!

07:18.910 --> 07:19.660
I'm going—

07:31.640 --> 07:33.600
Ippo!

07:37.600 --> 07:40.060
Ippo!

07:51.990 --> 07:54.740
Oh no, I have to get Ippo!

07:59.690 --> 08:02.000
What happened? You're soaked!

08:02.630 --> 08:04.990
He kept his promise.

08:06.700 --> 08:08.130
Dad...

08:13.850 --> 08:15.720
Dad came home.

08:30.810 --> 08:32.820
We have to live on, together.

08:36.070 --> 08:40.330
The Makunouchi Fishing Boat

08:37.950 --> 08:40.330
What kind of carpenters are
you? It's all crooked!

08:40.330 --> 08:42.430
You were rushing us!

08:42.430 --> 08:45.960
Every fisherman here's gonna give you
idiots a lashing if you do shoddy work!

08:46.670 --> 08:48.110
Mister Sakuma!

08:48.110 --> 08:49.090
Hey, Ippo!

08:49.930 --> 08:52.710
Look, mom got her boating license!

08:53.160 --> 08:54.720
"Boat operator."

08:54.720 --> 08:56.260
Nice work, Hiroko-san!

08:56.260 --> 08:59.180
Thank you. I finally got it on the third try.

08:59.180 --> 09:01.750
We'll show you where
all the best spots are.

09:01.750 --> 09:04.640
Your boat'll have a reputation
for guaranteed hauls!

09:04.640 --> 09:05.850
Thank you so much.

09:06.490 --> 09:07.850
Let's go, Ippo!

09:08.550 --> 09:10.610
You're heading out to sea right away?!

09:11.200 --> 09:12.580
We'll do our best!

09:14.730 --> 09:16.950
He'll be with us, too.

09:16.950 --> 09:19.650
Yeah... you're right.

09:19.650 --> 09:21.780
C'mon, Mom, let's go!

09:21.780 --> 09:22.770
Wait a minute!

09:22.770 --> 09:25.710
C'mon, c'mon!

09:25.710 --> 09:26.950
Nope, I'm too worried!

09:26.950 --> 09:27.890
Let's go with them!

09:27.890 --> 09:28.830
I'm in!

09:32.840 --> 09:33.810
Port side, check.

09:33.810 --> 09:35.840
Aren't you done yet?! Hurry up!

09:34.860 --> 09:35.840
Deck, check.

09:35.840 --> 09:38.340
Makunouchi Fishing Boat

09:37.520 --> 09:38.340
It's moving!

09:38.830 --> 09:40.500
Here we go, Ippo!

09:40.500 --> 09:41.220
Yeah!

09:41.220 --> 09:42.970
The Makunouchi Fishing Boat...

09:44.420 --> 09:47.020
has set sail!

09:50.290 --> 09:51.150
Ippo!

09:51.680 --> 09:52.980
Mom!

09:53.470 --> 09:55.760
Let's be strong, Ippo!

09:55.760 --> 09:57.980
Yeah, we'll be strong!

10:05.100 --> 10:09.420
I'm going to become even stronger...
until I finally catch up to Dad.

10:13.900 --> 10:15.960
First, I have to focus on my next defense.

10:19.800 --> 10:22.300
I will destroy the Dempsey Roll!

10:20.590 --> 10:22.300
So we've finally got a challenger

10:22.910 --> 10:26.220
who claims he can beat the Dempsey Roll.

10:26.620 --> 10:29.650
Ippo-kun's fourth title defense is against

10:30.060 --> 10:32.480
the Ryukyu warrior, Shimabukuro Iwao.

10:39.990 --> 10:42.360
Kamogawa Boxing Gym

10:43.120 --> 10:45.370
Use your hips.
Your punches are soft!

10:45.370 --> 10:47.870
Those punches won't even
make Shimabukuro flinch!

10:48.130 --> 10:50.960
Keep your hands moving.
More rotation!

10:50.960 --> 10:54.250
Wow, they're both fired up.

10:54.250 --> 10:56.000
And here's why.

10:56.980 --> 10:58.510
Destroy the Dempsey Roll?

10:58.510 --> 11:00.480
Ippo's own pain and suffering

11:00.480 --> 11:04.080
are what led him to develop
the Dempsey Roll on his own.

11:04.080 --> 11:06.010
If someone manages to stop it...

11:06.490 --> 11:08.770
It'll be a huge blow to him.

11:08.770 --> 11:11.520
I see. No wonder he's going all out.

11:11.930 --> 11:15.000
The Dempsey Roll won
me the championship.

11:15.000 --> 11:17.140
I have to keep refining it,

11:17.140 --> 11:19.030
until it's strong enough to beat anyone!

11:20.290 --> 11:22.200
Until it's perfect!

11:25.080 --> 11:28.500
It's been 13 minutes since he
went down... any second now...

11:33.330 --> 11:36.320
Shimabukuro, it's almost time to leave.

11:36.320 --> 11:37.610
Are you ready?

11:37.610 --> 11:38.590
Sure am, coach.

11:39.000 --> 11:40.430
I can't wait.

11:40.430 --> 11:43.190
This is my opportunity to
see if I really am strong,

11:43.190 --> 11:46.850
or if there are men out
there stronger than me.

11:47.510 --> 11:50.720
I heard Makunouchi-kun's
the son of a fisherman.

11:50.720 --> 11:52.990
That's correct.

11:52.990 --> 11:55.480
So he's a son of the sea, too.

11:56.100 --> 11:59.030
We'll see who the stronger son is.

11:59.930 --> 12:03.020
I'm going to drag him deep
down to the ocean floor.

12:03.710 --> 12:06.980
I'll face the hard-punching
champion Makunouchi Ippo head-on

12:06.980 --> 12:10.000
and go blow-for-blow with him
at the bottom of the sea.

12:11.120 --> 12:13.220
And that's where I'll win!

12:13.220 --> 12:17.590
I'll crush his trademark Dempsey Roll!

12:17.970 --> 12:18.790
Yeah!

12:18.790 --> 12:20.590
Iwao!

12:20.590 --> 12:22.970
Come back with the belt!

12:22.970 --> 12:25.630
The whole island will be celebrating!

12:25.630 --> 12:28.650
Win the title!

12:30.970 --> 12:32.370
I give you my word!

12:32.370 --> 12:36.370
On my honor as a son of the sea,
I'll come back with the big one!

12:37.770 --> 12:39.210
The wait is over, everyone!

12:39.210 --> 12:41.060
Beginning shortly at
the Champion's Carnival,

12:41.060 --> 12:44.000
it's the Japanese
featherweight title match!

12:41.170 --> 12:45.980
Makunouchi Ippo vs. Shimabukuro Iwao

12:49.710 --> 12:50.410
Senpai!

12:50.410 --> 12:51.520
How you feeling?

12:51.520 --> 12:52.330
Guys!

12:52.330 --> 12:55.000
Whoa, new trunks!

12:55.460 --> 12:58.770
Yeah, my mom and
Umezawa-kun made them.

12:59.470 --> 13:01.230
They look good on you, Ippo.

13:01.230 --> 13:02.760
Thanks, Kimura-san!

13:03.120 --> 13:05.340
Give it all you've got, Ippo-kun!

13:05.340 --> 13:08.760
Your fourth defense is the start
of a big run for the Kamogawa gym.

13:09.290 --> 13:11.310
Then Aoki's first title match,

13:11.310 --> 13:11.770
Yeah!

13:11.770 --> 13:14.140
Itagaki's Rookie King fight,

13:14.140 --> 13:17.440
and Takamura's first World title defense.

13:18.620 --> 13:21.680
It's up to you to start
things off right, kid!

13:21.680 --> 13:22.440
Sir!

13:22.960 --> 13:24.650
Good luck, senpai.

13:25.020 --> 13:26.320
Thanks.

13:26.320 --> 13:27.740
We'll be cheering.

13:27.740 --> 13:29.420
Kick his ass, Ippo!

13:29.420 --> 13:32.240
It'll give me momentum for my title match!

13:32.670 --> 13:34.000
I'll do my best!

13:34.000 --> 13:37.210
Don't worry about minor
crap like Aoki's fights.

13:37.210 --> 13:38.910
What?!

13:38.910 --> 13:41.750
Don't screw up before my title defense.

13:42.510 --> 13:43.420
Right.

13:46.800 --> 13:48.430
Okay, kid, let's go!

13:52.430 --> 13:53.300
Yes, sir!

13:57.740 --> 14:00.560
The challenger is now making
his way to the blue corner.

14:00.560 --> 14:03.060
Hailing from Okinawa,
the sea’s strongest son!

14:03.060 --> 14:05.900
13 fights. 12 wins,
all by KO. Only one loss.

14:05.900 --> 14:08.110
Ranked number one in the Japanese
featherweight division,

14:08.110 --> 14:10.320
Shimabukuro Iwao!

14:11.310 --> 14:12.200
What<i> is</i> that?

14:12.590 --> 14:14.110
He's a mountain of muscle!

14:14.110 --> 14:16.030
He's so big, he can't even lower his arms!

14:16.030 --> 14:18.340
How do you even get a body like that?!

14:18.340 --> 14:21.880
And now his opponent,
heading to the red corner.

14:21.880 --> 14:24.950
16 fights. 15 wins,
all by KO. Only one loss.

14:24.950 --> 14:27.590
The champion, Makunouchi Ippo!

14:27.590 --> 14:29.210
Get him, Makunouchi!

14:29.210 --> 14:30.770
Knock him out!

14:30.770 --> 14:32.190
Win!

14:32.190 --> 14:33.990
The two boxers come face to face.

14:33.990 --> 14:36.250
It's a battle between two hard punchers

14:36.250 --> 14:37.770
who've both won all their
fights by knockout!

14:38.200 --> 14:42.250
Now that I see them facing off,
I can see the height difference.

14:42.250 --> 14:46.120
This is the first time Ippo's had to
fight someone shorter than him.

14:46.120 --> 14:49.340
Short or not, Shimabukuro
is buff as hell.

14:49.340 --> 14:51.020
Look at how thick his neck is!

14:51.020 --> 14:53.530
He's not gonna be easy to take down.

14:53.530 --> 14:56.760
Will the champion successfully
defend his title for the fourth time,

14:56.760 --> 14:59.040
or will the belt be
flying down to Okinawa?

14:59.620 --> 15:02.040
Tonight he faces his strongest challenger!

15:02.040 --> 15:05.050
The first match of the Champion's
Carnival is about to begin!

15:05.920 --> 15:07.550
There's the bell!

15:10.410 --> 15:12.300
Both men begin by putting
up their guards,

15:12.300 --> 15:15.470
but the challenger's guard brings
him much lower to the ground!

15:15.900 --> 15:18.630
Shimabukuro-san is angling
to beat the Dempsey Roll.

15:19.300 --> 15:21.290
I can't risk using it carelessly.

15:21.290 --> 15:22.890
I'll start by feeling him out.

15:25.220 --> 15:27.420
Things are starting off surprisingly quiet.

15:27.420 --> 15:28.970
The title of Japan's strongest infighter

15:28.970 --> 15:31.880
is on the line in this bout, as well!

15:31.880 --> 15:35.290
The challenger made no bones about
his intent to best the Dempsey Roll.

15:35.290 --> 15:36.910
In a pre-fight interview,

15:36.910 --> 15:40.330
he vowed to "drag the champion
to the bottom of the sea."

15:40.330 --> 15:42.750
What could he have meant by that?

15:43.150 --> 15:45.000
What pressure...

15:45.450 --> 15:48.050
It's like he's pushing up at me from below.

15:48.380 --> 15:50.300
He's being pretty cautious.

15:50.300 --> 15:52.910
Well, if he won't move... I will!

15:52.910 --> 15:54.550
Shimabukuro makes a move!

15:54.550 --> 15:56.070
Here I come, Makunouchi-kun!

15:56.590 --> 15:57.930
A left from the champ!

15:58.240 --> 16:01.960
It feels like I got nailed with
a brick. What a hard left!

16:01.960 --> 16:03.100
And another left!

16:03.100 --> 16:04.790
So fast, so powerful!

16:04.790 --> 16:07.110
The champ's jabs feel more like straights!

16:07.620 --> 16:09.440
Atta boy, Makunouchi!

16:07.620 --> 16:11.610
He's got one hell of a left, but it
won't be enough to stop Shimabukuro!

16:09.440 --> 16:11.610
Wail on him!

16:12.110 --> 16:16.030
The champ continues throwing
lefts, but the challenger dodges!

16:16.030 --> 16:17.600
He's weaving low!

16:17.600 --> 16:20.530
The mountain of muscle makes
his way to the champ's chest!

16:20.530 --> 16:21.870
Uh-oh!

16:21.870 --> 16:24.920
A dead end! The pressure backs
the champ into the corner!

16:24.920 --> 16:28.860
All the showy outboxing doesn't suit you!

16:28.860 --> 16:30.690
Get ready to fight!

16:30.690 --> 16:33.690
He throws a hard left body blow!

16:33.690 --> 16:34.880
Wait, the champ blocked it!

16:35.430 --> 16:39.640
Now he returns fire! The champ
lands his signature liver blow!

16:39.640 --> 16:42.640
The challenger is frozen!
Is the champ on the offensive now?

16:43.010 --> 16:46.150
No, he's too low!
The champ can't follow up!

16:47.910 --> 16:50.900
A right out of nowhere!
What a huge swing!

16:51.410 --> 16:52.870
Watch out!

16:52.100 --> 16:53.700
Don't let him land that!

16:52.870 --> 16:54.400
He'll send you flying!

16:55.250 --> 16:56.840
I can't let him get in on me again!

16:57.850 --> 17:00.620
The champ tries for some breathing
room with a quick, tight combo!

17:00.620 --> 17:03.870
Back off, back off, back off!

17:05.170 --> 17:06.460
He's gone?!

17:06.460 --> 17:07.170
Below!

17:07.170 --> 17:09.120
The challenger gets even lower!

17:09.120 --> 17:11.070
That compact stance can
only mean one thing!

17:11.070 --> 17:12.820
No, don't let him connect!

17:12.820 --> 17:14.050
The punch is...

17:16.910 --> 17:18.560
A Gazelle punch!

17:18.560 --> 17:20.350
The cross-arm block is blasted apart!

17:20.660 --> 17:22.100
He's so strong!

17:22.100 --> 17:24.180
He can use the Gazelle punch, too?!

17:24.180 --> 17:26.940
No time to stand around shocked, kid!

17:27.320 --> 17:30.860
The challenger immediately follows
the Gazelle punch with a barrage!

17:30.860 --> 17:34.360
The champ can only defend.
He's trapped in the corner!

17:34.820 --> 17:37.780
A clean body blow!

17:38.330 --> 17:39.300
What do I do?

17:39.300 --> 17:41.790
Things will only get worse if I just block!

17:42.370 --> 17:43.620
Block?

17:43.620 --> 17:46.180
Forget about defense!

17:48.430 --> 17:50.780
The champ moves in!

17:50.780 --> 17:52.920
He's calling for full-on infight!

17:52.920 --> 17:55.590
That's it, Ippo.
That's your distance!

17:55.590 --> 17:59.590
Not many people will go toe-to-toe
with a power fighter.

17:59.590 --> 18:02.470
Shimabukuro won't be used
to fighting this close!

18:02.470 --> 18:06.160
Now it's fifty-fifty odds.
Get him, kid!

18:08.390 --> 18:11.140
Sparks fly as the two fighters
stick to one another like glue!

18:11.140 --> 18:13.690
Both their heads are
knocked this way and that!

18:14.200 --> 18:17.700
They're too close to get
a wind up or a big swing,

18:17.700 --> 18:20.450
so how can they still hit so hard?

18:20.450 --> 18:24.330
The power's coming from their hip
rotation and weight distribution.

18:24.680 --> 18:26.600
As long as they've got
a fist's worth of space,

18:26.600 --> 18:27.830
they can keep throwing those bombs.

18:28.390 --> 18:30.380
They're perfectly even.

18:30.380 --> 18:32.380
It's a battle of wills at this point.

18:32.380 --> 18:34.840
Keep punching!

18:35.230 --> 18:37.130
Move forward!

18:40.870 --> 18:44.060
There's the bell!
Round one is over!

18:51.460 --> 18:54.670
You were smart to slug it out.
Keep it up next round!

18:54.670 --> 18:55.320
Right!

18:55.320 --> 18:58.950
Don't let him push you around.
This is going to stay a battle of wills!

18:59.390 --> 19:02.210
The moment you back down
is the moment you lose!

19:02.210 --> 19:03.070
Right!

19:03.450 --> 19:05.600
He's got serious speed.

19:05.600 --> 19:08.810
But we've got the power advantage.

19:08.810 --> 19:10.460
Drive him into the ground, got it?

19:10.460 --> 19:10.960
Right!

19:12.710 --> 19:14.620
Makunouchi-kun is strong,

19:14.620 --> 19:17.600
but he took my invitation to brawl.

19:18.010 --> 19:19.970
Just like I planned.

19:21.660 --> 19:23.220
Round two!

19:23.220 --> 19:27.720
Both men fly out of their corners.
They're charging head-first!

19:28.150 --> 19:29.480
Body blow by the champ!

19:30.100 --> 19:32.730
The champ keeps him pinned
down at point-blank range!

19:33.150 --> 19:35.400
You're right where I want
you, Makunouchi-kun...

19:36.030 --> 19:39.150
Ankle deep in the ocean!

19:39.820 --> 19:43.490
An uppercut interrupts
the champ's barrage!

19:43.490 --> 19:47.650
It's a knock-down drag-out fight
in the center of the ring!

19:47.650 --> 19:49.770
They switch between offense and
defense at a blistering pace!

19:49.770 --> 19:51.730
Neither man pauses for a moment,

19:51.730 --> 19:54.750
nor does the crowd's cheering
through this climactic battle!

19:55.420 --> 19:57.840
The champ is managing to
throw a few more punches,

19:58.420 --> 20:01.230
but then a brutal strike
cuts his attacks short!

20:01.230 --> 20:03.950
If either pauses for a second, he's
sure to be pounded into submission!

20:03.950 --> 20:06.820
The tension is thick in the arena!

20:06.820 --> 20:09.100
A war of wills and fists
unfolds in the ring,

20:09.100 --> 20:12.350
as these two men compete for the
title of Japan's strongest infighter!

20:19.130 --> 20:22.490
Fifth round, and neither
man is giving an inch!

20:22.490 --> 20:25.990
Whose fists will finally
shatter the stalemate?!

20:25.990 --> 20:30.120
The champ connects with an uppercut! Shimabukuro's head flies back!

20:30.750 --> 20:31.830
He's waning!

20:31.830 --> 20:32.870
Put him away!

20:33.280 --> 20:34.460
The champ follows up!

20:34.460 --> 20:37.380
He rains down blows!
He's trying to end it!

20:37.380 --> 20:39.630
Hang on, Shimabukuro!

20:39.630 --> 20:42.630
One more push! Grit your teeth
and keep those hands moving!

20:47.070 --> 20:48.510
He's opening!

20:52.110 --> 20:55.480
The champ is met with a right!

20:55.480 --> 20:57.650
Damn it! Why'd he try for a big swing?!

20:57.650 --> 21:00.650
The champ stumbles backwards!

21:01.000 --> 21:03.930
If he'd just kept chipping
away, he would've won.

21:03.930 --> 21:05.650
C-Coach.

21:05.650 --> 21:07.600
Ippo-kun's face is turning...

21:10.330 --> 21:11.410
That's...

21:12.460 --> 21:15.920
Cyanosis, due to prolonged hypoxia!

21:16.990 --> 21:19.030
Can't... breathe...

21:19.510 --> 21:20.920
Body feels heavy...

21:20.920 --> 21:24.390
Welcome to the ocean floor.

22:46.010 --> 22:51.010
The Dempsey Roll Destroyed
